From d005a3950b60b586dc1acfcf648247df8b333fdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:31:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] prose_portal: Haiku's coding style, and nothing else

Includes in the guidelines' groups -- POSIX, the public driver API, then the
private headers -- in ASCII order within each; C++ casts for every C one,
static_cast where the source is void* so those are still checked, and
reinterpret_cast only between unrelated pointer types or for the buffer index
the virtqueue carries in its void* tag; lines kept within 100 columns; and doc
comments that close on their own line.

No change in behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0128-prose-portal-haiku-s-coding-style-and-nothing-else.patch c443377ec18461a7058e584f0d997c3214e777415cbe71903dac0b175f81321d
